Problem: AI Job Application Screening Pipeline
Build a backend that helps recruiters screen job applications using AI.

Requirements:
POST /jobs → create a job with a title and required skills list
POST /jobs/:id/apply → accept a resume as plain text, run it through an AI model to score how well it matches the job (0–100), extract matched skills, and store the result
GET /jobs/:id/applicants → return all applicants sorted by AI score descending
GET /jobs/:id/applicants/top → return only applicants scoring above 70
Background processing — AI scoring should happen async, applicant status starts as processing then updates to scored
Logging at every stage
Full unit tests

Task:
- POST /jobs : create jobs
- POST /jobs/:id/apply: To apply the job
    - Accept resume
    - Call extract API -> sync
    - return 200
    - call AI service -> Claude API / OpenAI API
    - Arch: 
        - User click apply -> Processing as default value
        - It calls the scoring API
        - Return status as scored
        Async
- GET /jobs/:id/applicants: return all applicants sorted by AI score descending
- GET /jobs/:id/applicants/top : return only applicants scoring above 70


Data Model
Jobs:
- Title: String: Mandatory
- Description: String: Mandatory
- Required Skills: []: Mandatory
- JobID: UUID: generated
- Applicants: generated

Resume:
- Matched Skills:[] 
- Extracted Skills: []: Non empty
- Unmatched Skills: []
- Score: 0-100
- ResumeId
- JobId
- ApplicantID
- ApplicationStatus: Processing default, statuses: Processing, Not proceeding, Scored

Applicants:
- Name
- ResumeId
- JobId
- ApplicantID


